  "findings": [
    "The phase verdict admits the unchanged normal condition, not all candidate artifacts or all saved prose. No demonstrated isolation, task-delivery, or expected-oracle defect requires a stop. Preserve host validation and all artifact failures.",
    "OpenCode executes no Beads memory query, capture, or recall in either isolated arm. Its continuation has implementation errors, premature ordinary stops, raw unexecuted tool markup, and a destructive git checkout of prior product code. These are measured behaviors; actual saved task delivery is present. Both continuation arms have zero fully passing artifacts.",
    "Zcode passes every isolated frozen artifact in both arms. Stage4 treatment retrieves the prior frozen endpoint note in both families, and stage5 reconciliation retrieves the new cutoff note. These are search\u2192preview\u2192full-read routes; code, docs and issues also supply the facts, so correctness is not attributed causally to memory.",
    "Initial stage1 treatment capture opportunities: OpenCode0/2, zcode0/2. Revision stage4: OpenCode0/2, zcode2/2; zcode performs3 writes across those2 opportunities because it also updates the renewable frozen-note implementation description. Baseline capture is0/2 initial and0/2 revision per host.",
    "Stage3 treatment writes occur in both zcode families and neither OpenCode family. Both add useful permanent frozen-endpoint scope rather than duplicating an existing captured agreement; initial policy capture omissions remain separate. No observed duplicate unchanged-record capture is established.",
    "Eligible stages2/5/6: treatment12 slots have11 search commands in4 sessions,1 actual prior-record full read,0 known-reference direct reads, and4 same-session write-verification recalls. Baseline12 slots have0 of all routes. Of the4 search sessions, reconciliation2 searches before implementation but finds no match; renewals5 and reconciliation6 search after implementation to prepare captures; reconciliation5 reads prior cutoff before edits.",
    "Revision stage4 treatment4 slots have7 searches,2 prior-record full reads,0 known-reference direct reads,3 same-session verification recalls. Control stage3 treatment4 slots have3 searches,0 prior reads,2 verification recalls. No search result returns a full record; matching results are truncated previews.",
    "Zcode reconciliation CSV note remains byte-identical through stages3\u20136. Its CR rationale is false on the pinned Python3.14.7 runtime, and the future-export hand-escaper mandate is unsupported. Stage4/5 searches surface only a preview before the false rationale; neither recalls the CSV body. Code reads expose the old false comment, but the escaper remains unchanged and further library-avoidance reliance is unobserved. Do not generalize the issue to Python3.13 or infer how the agent formed it.",
    "Zcode frozen endpoint and current numerical/date policies remain accurate and scoped through revisions. The no-refactor mandate in the replay note is stronger than the business requirement; the renewal current-policy note phrase survives only in support_replay becomes stale after compat_notice is introduced. No historical numerical policy is overwritten in memory.",
    "Zcode public-test notes have useful supersession conclusions with provenance defects. The renewal note overclaims a before/after verification that git stash did not isolate to the current stage. The final reconciliation note incorrectly says stage4 moved daily_net (introduced at5); its stage1\u20133 verification claim exceeds the executed loop, which stops at1, although read identical old cases support the inference. Earlier unaffected/frozen cases remain valid; only superseded active expectations are obsolete.",
    "Naturally authored factual memory-key attributions appear in zcode reconciliation stage4/5 closing reasons. They contain no lookup instruction and are not original task contamination. Later stages do not read those issue records, so no direct-reference exposure/use is established. The daily note also cross-references the cutoff record.",
    "OpenCode renewal baseline corrupts the frozen endpoint at4; treatment at6 invents current values as release1 despite original issue history remaining available. OpenCode baseline reconciliation stage4 git checkout removes refunds_csv and incident_replay from the product. These are candidate code/prose failures, not deletion prescribed by tasks or performed by the auditor.",
    "One OpenCode continuation host_success=false is retained separately from infrastructure_fault=false. The sole message without an assistant model row is explicitly synthetic metadata.compaction_continue at stream line142. Both adjacent assistant stops have pinned Qwen rows; no tool follows that continuation. Preserve frozen stream-validation failure; evidence bounds the concern without establishing a different model or absent task delivery.",
    "Uniform posthoc supplemental coverage40/40 uses preserved candidate snapshots and independent stage-specific references in separate fresh readonly sandboxes on the pinned runtime.32pass;5 OpenCode treatment reconciliation2\u20136 fail absolute-instant ordering;3 OpenCode baseline reconciliation4\u20136 fail because the CSV operation is absent. This is finite frozen coverage plus already graded missing-operation behavior, not wrong frozen expected cases. Never replace frozen grades with supplements."
  ],
